# Bluetooth's runs (BT=1): what is up once the daemons have had their start, and bt_test -- the state
# CoreBluetooth reports and a scan, which is also what wakes bluetoothd through launchd (it is on-demand
# here). Settings -> Bluetooth is the switch and the device list; the psgrep lines say whether
# bluetoothd, BlueTool and the keybag daemons are running without touching the screen.
# The kern.exec_inject line is the insertion list as the kernel holds it now (psgrep -sysctl; the
# probe library's lines -- "probe: NAME (pid N): ..." -- then say which processes actually got it).
/redwood/bin/tolog /redwood/bin/psgrep -sysctl kern.exec_inject
sleep 60
/redwood/bin/tolog /redwood/bin/psgrep bluetoothd BlueTool keybagd wifid securityd
/redwood/bin/tolog /redwood/bin/bt_test 30
sleep 30
/redwood/bin/tolog /redwood/bin/psgrep bluetoothd BlueTool keybagd
/redwood/bin/tolog /redwood/bin/bt_test 30

